# Kazana — Product Vision (always apply)

Kazana is an **AI Hiring Intelligence Platform**.

It is **NOT** a job board, ATS, interview-question repository, recruiter CRM, or generic interview platform.

## Moat

- The **assessment engine** is the primary product and long-term moat.
- Candidate products exist to create value and **learning signals**.
- Enterprise products **monetize** the calibrated assessment engine.
- Enterprise workflow data **strengthens** the assessment engine.
- Candidates and enterprises reinforce one another.

## Decision filter

Before building or suggesting a feature, ask:

> Does this naturally strengthen the assessment engine or one of its learning loops?

If no, push back or redesign. Also ask: does this improve our ability to make better hiring decisions over time?

## Flywheel (strengthen, don't break)

Jobs → Resume Optimization → AI Interview Practice → Real Interview → Interview Experience Submission → Assessment Improvement → Better AI Interviews → More Users

- Jobs = acquisition/retention, **not** differentiation.
- Resume Optimization = interview readiness.
- AI Interviews = flagship B2C experience.
- Interview reports are **confidence-scored** (probabilistic)—avoid binary verified/unverified as the primary model.

## Engineering / AI defaults

- Prefer **reusable structured data**, **confidence-aware** outputs, **explainability**, and **calibration**.
- Do **not** re-parse raw job descriptions in matching/filters; consume canonical extraction / facets / tags.
- Keep AI **provider-agnostic** (adapters, versioned prompts, replaceable models).
- Use AI where it measurably improves hiring quality—not for novelty.
- Every architectural choice should support **long-term learning**.

